Do not let:

ONE ANOMALY
->
NEW THEORY.

DECISION
AR-H98 is POSITIVE WITH A DIAGNOSTIC-COST / STRUCTURAL-MODEL LIMIT.

Supported synthetically:

- structured residual error can seed a new provisional model;
- an independent validation batch sharply suppresses false birth;
- known-regime noise produces very low false promotion;
- transient novelty does not survive validation;
- promoted models recover useful action structure;
- model birth repays its cost in the tested persistent novel regime;
- retained newborn models provide large recurrence value.

Not demonstrated:

- structural causal hypothesis generation;
- continuous/high-dimensional state;
- optimal diagnostic sampling;
- online local model splitting/merging;
- model-memory pricing;
- distributed hypothesis birth across cells.

